          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Estimated number of days if it flies 900 km/day = 12,000 ÷ 900 = 13.3 days"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.144,
            0.804,
            0.182
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Estimated number of days if it flies 1000 km/day = 12,000 ÷ 1000 = 12 days"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.183,
            0.823,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence it would take approximately 12 to 14 days for a grey headed albatross to complete a 12,000 km trip to cross an ocean."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.242,
            0.884,
            0.341
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13.A bar-tailed godwit holds the record for the longest recorded non-stop flight. It travelled 13,560 km from Alaska to Australia without stopping. Its journey started on 13 October 2022 and continued for about 11 days. Find out the approximate distance it covered every day. Find out the approximate distance it covered every hour.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.354,
            0.23,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.372,
            0.891,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Distance covered per day = 13,560 km ÷ 11 days = 1232.73 km or 1233 km. Distance covered per hour = 1233 ÷ 24 = 51.36 km or 51 km."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.426,
            0.884,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14.Bald eagles are known to fly as high as 4500 – 6000 m above the ground level. Mount Everest is about 8850 m high. Aeroplanes can fly as high as 10,000 – 12,800 m. How many times bigger are these heights compared to Somu’s building?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.524,
            0.864,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Height of Somu’s building = 40 m (i) Bald eagles’ flight height = 4500 – 6000 m Lower estimate = 4500 ÷ 40 = 112.5 times Upper estimate = 6000 ÷ 40 = 150 times Bald eagles fly about 112 to 150 times higher than Somu’s building."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.658,
            0.882,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Mount Everest height = 8850 m Now, 8850 ÷ 40 = 221.25 Mount Everest is approximately 221 times taller than Somu’s building."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.755,
            0.828,
            0.836
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Aeroplanes flight height = 10,000 – 12,000 m Lower estimate = 10,000 ÷ 40 = 250 Upper estimate = 12800 ÷ 40 = 320. Airplanes fly about 250 to 320 times as high as Somu’s building."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
